# Project npm config (web/dashboard) - the root npmrc law, mirrored here:
# when the dashboard Pages project (vant-brain) roots npm at this dir, it
# reads THIS file, not the repo root's. Same rationale as the root law
# (npm/cli#9787): the npm 10.x arborist optional-peer-set crash fires on
# this graph's @vitejs/devtools shape under registry drift on npm 10.9.x -
# reproduced verbatim locally on the builder's exact stack (node 20.20.0 +
# npm 10.9.2, "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')")
# during an npm install path over a stale lockfile. The crashes were
# really two-legged: (1) the lock was stale against the manifest, forcing
# npm into ideal-tree rebuild - FIXED by re-syncing package-lock.json to
# the exact pins; (2) the flag keeps any future drift from the arborist
# bug instead of the crash. No-op for npm ci against complete lockfiles;
# bun installs never touch this file.
legacy-peer-deps=true
